{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to boot persistently with `audit=1`. After a safe reboot, the boot ID changed, the live kernel command line contains exactly one `audit=1`, and kernel auditing reports enabled. RHEL 10.0, the installed kernel, services, access, and protected account data were preserved. The pre-existing disabled auditd service was not altered.","actions_performed":["Used the installed RHEL `grubby` tool to add `audit=1` to all boot entries and GRUB defaults.","Restarted node1 once using the native safe reboot mechanism.","Verified post-reboot kernel auditing, persistent configuration, service recovery, administrative access, and cleanup."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Kernel boots with audit=1 and retains it across reboots","command_ids":["cmd-d56ca2a5b4f54e08","cmd-449b4b581634466e","cmd-c9758a76e2d14f9a"],"summary":"Boot entries and GRUB defaults contain exactly one `audit=1`; after reboot `/proc/cmdline` includes it and `auditctl -s` reports `enabled 1`."},{"requirement":"Installed operating-system release and kernel remain unchanged","command_ids":["cmd-42891685965f443f","cmd-449b4b581634466e"],"summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 match before and after the change."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-42891685965f443f","cmd-a7e51d859510494c","cmd-ca01943e8e5c49c0","cmd-449b4b581634466e"],"summary":"Baseline boot ID was 6ab6a71b-188c-48ae-971b-a6bb378b1d72; safe reboot was acknowledged; recovered boot ID is a57b9526-59ef-4b0b-9e75-7a592fb44ae3; SSH and chronyd recovered with no failed units."},{"requirement":"Administrative access and protected data preserved","command_ids":["cmd-14a45e327ec344e7","cmd-449b4b581634466e","cmd-c9758a76e2d14f9a"],"summary":"SSH remains active and listening, while `/etc/passwd` and `/etc/shadow` checksums match their pre-change values."},{"requirement":"Cleanup completed","command_ids":["cmd-e82aa323253a455f"],"summary":"No transient benchmark reboot units remain; the final live audit and service checks succeeded."}]}
